{title: 647 - Mine Eyes Have Seen the Glory}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #647 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 647}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Mine eyes have seen the glory of the coming [Eb/Bb]of the Lord;
[Eb]He is [Bb]trampling out the vintage where the grapes of wrath are stored;
[Bb]He hath loosed the [Cm/Eb]fateful [F/C]lightning [Gm/D]of [Bb]his terrible swift sword;
[Bb]His truth is marching on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Eb/Bb]Glory! Glory! [Bb]Hallelujah! Glory! Glory! Hallelujah!
[Bb/F]Glory! Glory! Hallelujah! [Cm/Eb]His truth [Gm/D]is marching on.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]He has sounded forth the trumpet that shall never [Eb/Bb]call retreat;
[Eb]He is [Bb]sifting out the hearts of men before His judgment seat;
[Bb]O be swift, [Cm/Eb]my soul, [Gm/D]to [F/C]answer [Gm/D]Him! [Bb]be jubilant, my feet!
[Bb]Our God is marching on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]In the beauty of the lilies Christ was born [Eb/Bb]across the sea,
[Eb]With a [Bb]glory in His bosom that transfigures you and me;
[Bb]As He died [Cm/Eb]to make [Gm/D]men [F/C]holy, [Gm/D]let [Bb]us live to make men free!
[Bb]While God is marching on.
{end_of_verse}
